<title>USA: Chateau Properties stake cut by N.Y. firm.</title>
<headline>Chateau Properties stake cut by N.Y. firm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oppenheimer &amp; Co Inc, based in New York, said Thursday it cut its stake in Chateau Properties Inc to 78,800 common shares or 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, Oppenheimer said its latest transactions include the sale of 346,000 common shares sold on January 29 at a price of $26.50 per share.</p>
<p>Chateau, based in Clinton Township, Mich., is a real estate investment trust which owns, manages, develops and acquires manufactured housing communities.</p>
</text>
